1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,120
One rysh session. In a moment, four
Claude agents will go to work inside it.

2
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:10,480
Three lanes: planning on the left,

3
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:13,520
the builders in the middle,
the shared board on the right.

4
00:00:18,465 --> 00:00:20,545
The roadmap agent goes first,

5
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:23,745
and its very first act is to
tell the board what this demo is.

6
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:31,520
Then the other three check in. Standing
by. Nobody has been given any work yet.

7
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:38,960
The roadmap writes the goal down: a todo
manager that runs entirely in the browser.

8
00:00:39,215 --> 00:00:42,255
No backend, no build step, no dependencies.

9
00:00:47,055 --> 00:00:51,375
It posts the deliverable, then hands
the whole thing to the fleet manager.

10
00:00:51,535 --> 00:00:53,215
That is the last order it gives.

11
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:02,400
The manager splits the work by layer.

12
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:06,960
Worker one takes the markup and the
styling, worker two takes all of the logic.

13
00:01:12,005 --> 00:01:17,125
But first it writes a contract: the six
element ids both halves must agree on.

14
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:19,765
That is what stops two
parallel agents from colliding.

15
00:01:26,150 --> 00:01:27,350
Contract posted.

16
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:30,870
Now the work orders go out, one to
each worker, and the build starts.

17
00:01:38,085 --> 00:01:39,445
Watch the middle lane.

18
00:01:39,605 --> 00:01:43,285
Both workers are running at once, and
neither has read the other's file.

19
00:01:43,685 --> 00:01:46,565
The contract is the only
thing holding them together.

20
00:01:58,070 --> 00:02:00,122
Worker one is done: the
page and the stylesheet,

21
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:03,375
checked back against the contract, id by id.

22
00:02:24,925 --> 00:02:29,245
Worker two finishes the logic. Add,
toggle, delete, clear completed,

23
00:02:29,245 --> 00:02:32,205
a live count, and the list
persisted to local storage.

24
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:45,180
Notice that neither worker
reported back by message.

25
00:02:45,340 --> 00:02:47,980
They posted to the board, and
the manager has been watching

26
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:51,340
it, because a post cannot
be missed and a message can.

27
00:02:56,985 --> 00:02:59,145
Now the manager verifies for itself.

28
00:02:59,145 --> 00:03:03,065
Every id lines up, the page loads
both files, the syntax is clean.

29
00:03:03,065 --> 00:03:04,025
Then it signs off.

30
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:17,480
The roadmap checks the work against its
own acceptance list and closes the demo.

31
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:20,280
Four agents, one board, a working app.

32
00:03:25,425 --> 00:03:27,025
And all four have signed off.

